- Use Mermaid for creating maintainable diagrams and visualizations as code.
- Choose appropriate diagram types (flowchart, sequence, class, ERD) for different use cases.
- Use clear and descriptive node labels and relationship descriptions.
- Apply consistent styling and theming for professional diagram appearance.
- Structure complex diagrams with proper grouping and subgraphs for clarity.
- Use appropriate arrow types and line styles to convey different relationships.
- Implement proper version control for diagrams by storing them as text.
- Include diagrams in documentation workflows with automated rendering.
- Use Mermaid live editor for rapid prototyping and collaborative diagram design.
- Export diagrams to various formats (SVG, PNG, PDF) for different documentation needs.

